# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Desk-Buddy .gitignore
#
# Goals:
#   1. Keep compiled firmware artifacts out of the repository. Arduino/ESP32
#      builds are large, machine-specific, and fully reproducible from source.
#   2. Keep OS and editor metadata out of the history.
#   3. Keep credentials (Wi-Fi SSIDs, API tokens for future network features)
#      out of the history permanently -- a secret committed once stays in the
#      git objects forever, so it is excluded before any such file exists.
#   4. Keep audio media out of the repository. The microSD card content is
#      binary, large, and the redistribution rights of the source clips are
#      not established. See docs/audio.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Arduino / PlatformIO / ESP32 build output ---
build/
.build/
*.bin
*.elf
*.hex
*.map
*.d
*.o
*.a
*.su
.pio/
.pioenvs/
.piolibdeps/
# Arduino IDE 2.x per-sketch generated metadata
firmware/**/build/
sketch/

# --- Secrets and local configuration ---
# Any file matching these patterns is assumed to hold credentials and must
# never be committed. Commit a *.example counterpart instead.
secrets.h
credentials.h
arduino_secrets.h
*.secret
*.secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Audio media (see docs/audio.md) ---
# The DFPlayer Mini reads these directly from the microSD card; the repo
# documents the required layout rather than shipping the files.
*.mp3
*.wav
*.ogg
*.flac
sdcard/

# --- Large binary media that belongs in a release, not the history ---
*.mov
*.mp4
*.zip
*.tar.gz

# --- OS metadata ---
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Editor / IDE ---
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.cache/
compile_commands.json
